#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: sea
#> pause: 45
#> must: In Xanadu did Kubla Khan a stately pleasure dome decree
#> must: Down to a sunless sea.
#> not: Khan \
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: s/\\\n//
# 13. Join lines that end in a backslash. Pement: sed -e :a -e '/\\$/N; s/\\\n//; ta'
# When the line ends in \ (written \\ because \ is special), N pulls in the
# next line, s removes the backslash and the newline between them, and t
# loops back in case the joined line also ends in a backslash.
# Try: delete the  ta  and a run of three continued lines joins only two.
:a
/\\$/N; s/\\\n//; ta

#DATA
In Xanadu did Kubla Khan \
a stately pleasure dome decree
Where Alph, \
the sacred river, \
ran
Down to a sunless sea.
